IME 0.9 (Zvvm) for QEMU 11.1.1 -- generated by the ime-0.9-pipeline
(scripts/ime/qemu-ime, apply-qemu.mjs) against the v11.1.1 tag, with the
decode patterns apply-qemu.mjs skips because of its MARK-guard bug appended
by hand.  Adds the x-zvvmm/x-zvvfmm/x-zvvmtls/x-zvvmttls CPU properties
(default off), the tile load/store and matrix multiply-accumulate helpers,
and vsetlambda.  Also takes the vector unit to the RVV 1.0 maximum: RV_VLEN_MAX
1024 -> 65536 with the vlen property widened to 32 bits, the generic-vector
descriptor's size field widened (tcg-gvec-desc.h, 8 to 13 bits: operands up to
64 KB, not 2 KB, were silently truncated), the unit-stride and whole-register
load/store helpers looping over pages instead of assuming two, and the tile
helper buffers on the heap sized for a whole m8 group (test/riscv-vlen-probe
checks every instruction family at every VLEN).  Applied by deps/sniper-deps
for the riscv-ime feature; regenerate with tools/riscv/regen-qemu-patch.sh.
Regenerate from the pipeline when the specification moves.

