+/*
+ * ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
+ * Emulating an instruction-set extension from a plugin.
+ * (QEMU_PLUGIN_HAS_INSN_CLAIM says these four calls exist.)
+ *
+ * A plugin that implements instructions QEMU does not know (an accelerator
+ * extension under development) needs four things beyond the tracing API:
+ * to claim such an instruction at translation time so the block continues
+ * through it instead of ending in an illegal-instruction exception, to
+ * raise an architectural exception when the emulated instruction must trap,
+ * to expose the extension's registers through the gdbstub register list
+ * (so gdb and qemu_plugin_read_register see them), and to back system
+ * registers (RISC-V CSRs) that the extension defines.
+ */
